[CENTER]
[SIZE=7][B][COLOR=#2F80ED]NexDiscordLink[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][B]Secure Minecraft–Discord account linking, synchronization, 2FA, rewards, chat, and network support.[/B][/SIZE]

[COLOR=#2ECC71][B]Spigot/Paper 1.16.5+[/B][/COLOR] • [COLOR=#F39C12][B]Java 17+[/B][/COLOR] • [B]English & Turkish[/B]
[/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#2F80ED]More than a chat bridge[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

NexDiscordLink connects Discord to the complete Minecraft account lifecycle. Players can securely link their accounts, protect them with TOTP two-factor authentication, verify changed network addresses through Discord, synchronize roles and nicknames, receive configurable rewards, and use a two-way chat bridge.

It works on a single Spigot/Paper server with SQLite or across Velocity/Bungee backend servers with shared MySQL.

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#2F80ED]Account linking[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Link through a Discord DM, an interactive button/modal panel, or slash commands
[*]English and Turkish Minecraft commands and Discord slash commands
[*]One Minecraft account ↔ one Discord account policy
[*]Expiring, single-use link codes
[*]Rate-limited verification attempts
[*]Secure unlinking through TOTP or a short-lived Discord confirmation button
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#2F80ED]Account security[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]TOTP two-factor authentication
[*]In-game QR map for authenticator setup
[*]Private Discord verification when a player's network address changes
[*]AES-GCM encryption for stored TOTP secrets
[*]Non-reversible keyed fingerprints for stored IP addresses
[*]Automatic redaction of IP, token, secret, and key values in audit logs
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#2F80ED]Role, nickname, and ban synchronization[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Automatically assign a Discord role after account linking
[*]Synchronize Vault groups and Discord roles
[*]Minecraft → Discord, Discord → Minecraft, or bidirectional modes
[*]Synchronize on join, on a configurable schedule, or through an administrator command
[*]Synchronize Minecraft names with Discord nicknames
[*]Optional ban synchronization
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#2F80ED]Rewards and engagement[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Configurable account-link rewards
[*]Separate first-link and relink rewards
[*]Additional rewards based on Discord roles
[*]Recurring salary rewards for linked online players
[*]Discord server-boost rewards
[*]Run economy, item, XP, or third-party plugin commands together
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#2F80ED]Discord messaging and chat[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Bidirectional Minecraft ↔ Discord chat bridge
[*]Optional webhook usernames and Minecraft head avatars
[*]Join, quit, death, and advancement notifications
[*]Custom profile, linking, security, and audit embeds
[*]Per-message channel, title, description, color, author, thumbnail, image, footer, timestamp, and button settings
[*]Safe placeholders such as [ICODE]{player}[/ICODE], [ICODE]{uuid}[/ICODE], [ICODE]{message}[/ICODE], and [ICODE]{advancement}[/ICODE]
[*]Discord mention parsing disabled for bridged chat by default
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#2F80ED]Automatic Config Doctor and Lang Doctor[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

No command is required. NexDiscordLink automatically inspects the configuration and selected language file during startup and plugin reload.

[LIST]
[*]Detects invalid YAML, unknown settings, missing settings, and incorrect value types
[*]Checks ranges, Discord IDs, HTTP/HTTPS URLs, embed colors, and button styles
[*]Checks proxy/MySQL compatibility and missing feature dependencies
[*]Finds missing language keys and broken placeholders
[*]Never prints bot tokens, database passwords, or webhook values
[*]Reports clear ERROR, WARNING, or healthy summaries in the server console
[*]Does not rewrite your files or disable the plugin by itself
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#2F80ED]Network and storage support[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]SQLite for standalone servers
[*]MySQL for standalone or network deployments
[*]Shared-MySQL linking across Velocity/Bungee backend servers
[*]One designated bot node with lightweight worker backends
[*]PlaceholderAPI integration with an asynchronous cache
[*]Optional Vault integration
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#2F80ED]Commands[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

[B]Minecraft examples[/B]
[LIST]
[*][ICODE]/link[/ICODE] — aliases: [ICODE]/eşle[/ICODE], [ICODE]/hesapeşle[/ICODE], [ICODE]/esle[/ICODE], [ICODE]/hesapesle[/ICODE]
[*][ICODE]/unlink[/ICODE] — securely remove an account link
[*][ICODE]/linkstatus[/ICODE] — view account and 2FA status
[*][ICODE]/linkreward[/ICODE] — preview link rewards
[*][ICODE]/2fa setup|login|disable[/ICODE] — manage two-factor authentication
[*][ICODE]/nexdiscord status|reload|sync|resetreward[/ICODE] — administration
[/LIST]

[B]Discord examples[/B]
[LIST]
[*][ICODE]/link[/ICODE] / [ICODE]/eşle[/ICODE]
[*][ICODE]/profile[/ICODE] / [ICODE]/hesap[/ICODE]
[*][ICODE]/unlink[/ICODE] / [ICODE]/eşlemeyi-kaldır[/ICODE]
[*][ICODE]/help[/ICODE] / [ICODE]/yardım[/ICODE]
[*][ICODE]/setup-link[/ICODE]
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#2F80ED]Requirements[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Java 17 or newer
[*]Spigot or Paper 1.16.5 or newer
[*]A Discord bot with the required privileged intents
[*]Optional: Vault and a compatible permissions plugin
[*]Optional: PlaceholderAPI
[*]MySQL reachable from every backend when proxy mode is enabled
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#2F80ED]Quick setup[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

[LIST=1]
[*]Place the JAR in the server's [ICODE]plugins[/ICODE] folder.
[*]Start the server once, then stop it completely.
[*]Configure the bot token, channel IDs, and role IDs.
[*]Enable Server Members Intent and Message Content Intent in the Discord Developer Portal.
[*]Grant the bot the permissions required by the features you enable.
[*]Start the server and review the automatic Doctor report.
[*]Run [ICODE]/setup-link[/ICODE] in Discord if modal linking is enabled.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#2F80ED]Important security note[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

Never publish a live bot token, database password, webhook URL, production configuration, or [ICODE]secret.key[/ICODE]. The optional Discord console command is disabled by default and only executes explicitly allowlisted root commands when enabled.

